HashMaps:
1. LC:387 first unique character in the string
    - Create the frequency map
    - Iterate over the string if map.get(ch) == 1 return the index
    - If after iteration the code reaches the end return -1 that means no unique character
    - TC: O(N) SC: O(N)

2. Ransom Notes
   - We have two strings ransom='aa' magazine='aab' we need to return true if ransom is created by magazine false if not
   - Create [have] frequency map from magazine and [need] map from ransom
   - Iterate over the ransom string for each character in the ransom string
             - get the frequency of need character
             - for the same need character get the frequency of have
             - check if have < need return false eventually return true

   - TC: O(N) SC: O(N)

3. LC:1189 Max Balloons
   - similar to ransom note but in this ques we need to find the number of times we can make the balloon string
   - first create need -> balloon ka freq map and have -> string ka freq map
   - ab intuition ke hisaab se we need to find out the number of times we can use a particular character
             - for that do have[i]/need[i]
   - after the previous step we need to find the min of all the frequencies of the balloon
   - TC: O(n) SC: O(n)

4. LC:409 Longest palindrome
   - is question mein hme ek string de rakhi hogi hme find out krna hai max length ki palindrome string
   - thinking start kro yaha se ki 2 tarah ki string palindrome hoskti hai even length and odd length
   - even length ki palindrome string mein -> cabbac
   - odd length ki palindrome string mein -> even length ki palindrome string + in between any character but odd number of times
   - TC:O(n) SC:O(n)